# build_backend.py is the in-tree PEP 517 backend (pyproject.toml's
# build-backend / backend-path); setuptools never auto-includes root-level
# modules outside the package tree in an sdist, so without this an
# `sdist`-based install fails with "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named
# 'build_backend'" before the wheel build even starts.
include build_backend.py

# ui/ is not a Python package, so setuptools' package auto-discovery never picks it up --
# without this, the sdist ships without ui/ at all, so build_backend.py's _build_ui() (which
# checks for ui/package.json) silently no-ops even when npm is available, and `uv build`
# (which builds the wheel from the sdist, not the working tree) produces a wheel with no
# emergentflow/_static/ (ADR 0013, server falls back to the v0 demo page).
graft ui
prune ui/node_modules
prune ui/dist
global-exclude *.tsbuildinfo
graft agents
